  "sourceBoundContracts": [
    "Native SwRowFrame is an original SwClient registered at its row format; GetFormat reads this registration and height resolution uses the exact native frame-size item.",
    "Native ClaimFrameFormat moves all actual SwRowFrame clients for the claiming original row directly before re-registering that model row, leaving frames of peer rows unchanged.",
    "Native ChgFrameFormat emits TableLineFormatChanged with borrowed new-format/original-line references before row registration. SaveTable NewFrameFormatForLine emits the distinct MoveTableLineHint, directly registers the row and invokes KillEmptyFrameFormat.",
    "Native SwRowFrame DestroyImpl and SwTableLine destruction release their registration and delete a format only after its final represented client. Destructive row/table removal tears down the represented flat row frame clients before row model registration ends; ordinary nondestructive RemoveLine remains detachable.",
    "Mounted WriterEditableTable rendering and SwRootFrame measurement use direct registered native row-frame item reads and release temporary clients in finally. Original native rows, boxes, text and document cursor remain the owners throughout repeated attribute and numeric history.",
    "Full physical layout tree, native invalidation, follows/repeat frames, pooling, nested/merged table, UNO and modified-state contracts remain unverified. Flat teardown is a represented subset of native DelFrames, not complete hierarchical destruction.",
    "All prior316 metadata records/states/defaults/classifications/evidence prefixes and649 unaffected prior acceptance files stay unchanged except append-only bounded metadata notes; two old history cases capture expected construction values before native destruction without weakening literal/identity/history assertions. Registered IO/recovery deviations, whole writer-view source and stash remain unchanged; the full goal remains incomplete."
  ]
